#!/bin/sh
snapshot="$("$HOME/.local/bin/antonina-scheduler-snapshot" 2>/dev/null || printf '{}')"
exec timeout -k 15s 900s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant low --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-SCHEDULER-TURN. Optimize wall-clock time by topology. Use CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.
FIRST ACTION: breadth. While unrepresented_projects is nonempty, inspect ONLY CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.unrepresented_issues; skip represented-project issue reads. After one non-launch in a missing project, switch projects before another read there. CANDIDATE BUDGET: one compact issue read and at most one worktree lookup; never reread a skipped candidate.
Run antonina-scheduler-issue --issue ISSUE. Explicit complete/human/dependency blocker => skip immediately WITHOUT a worktree lookup. Else run antonina-scheduler-worktrees --issue ISSUE. [] => next. A returned cwd is registered, existing, and unoccupied: LAUNCH before another candidate. Unclear scope => bounded reconnaissance.
PRE-LAUNCH GATE: before second-agent/depth launch rerun antonina-scheduler-snapshot. If any project is newly unrepresented, continue from project breadth.
For a launch use ONE transaction:
antonina-scheduler-launch --issue ISSUE --cwd CWD --title TITLE --summary SUMMARY --prompt PROMPT --json
It revalidates the chosen registered/unoccupied cwd, generates the collision-resistant ID, creates+runs the detached agent, cleans up a failed create/run, and records the working claim only after run succeeds. Never call agent new/run directly from the scheduler. Never reuse a live cwd. Never use ls/find/globs over /workspace to discover cwd.
LIVE OWNERSHIP: CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.live_agents is authoritative. Never scan historical/finished agent inventories. A serialized queue with no live owner may get one bounded reconciliation owner on an unoccupied registered cwd.
BREADTH BARRIER: no project gets a second live agent until every project_hint is represented or precisely dependency/topology/collision-blocked. AFTER BREADTH: do not idle. Search represented_issue_candidates for positive-speedup distinct issues; after 2 skips in one project, switch projects before more reads. Then consider complementary intra-issue fronts. AssemblyP1 should have at least five useful agents whenever five independent positive-speedup fronts exist. Choose only actions with positive expected marginal wall-clock speedup after dependencies, overlap, collision risk, and reconciliation cost. AFTER EACH ACTION: refresh snapshot, treat it as CURRENT_SNAPSHOT, and restart breadth. IDLE WATCH only if both sweeps find no launch: all unrepresented projects represented/blocked, and represented_issue_candidates produced no launchable distinct issue or complementary front. Then sleep 20, refresh, retry until watchdog/fatal error.
CURRENT_SNAPSHOT:
$snapshot"
